Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:49:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Accept the configured PENNY_TOPIC_* secret naming

The six penny topic secrets were provisioned as PENNY_TOPIC_EARLY,
PENNY_TOPIC_CONFIRMING, PENNY_TOPIC_READY, PENNY_TOPIC_CIRCUIT_RISK,
PENNY_TOPIC_PORTFOLIO and PENNY_TOPIC_SYSTEM. The delivery module was reading
PENNY_<KIND>_TOPIC_ID, so every topic silently resolved to None and all four
sections would have posted to the chat root instead of their own threads.

Rather than require six configured secrets to be renamed, both conventions are
accepted. PENNY_TOPIC_* is primary because it reads more clearly and matches the
topic titles in the group; the older form remains a fallback. RADAR maps from
PENNY_TOPIC_EARLY and CIRCUIT from PENNY_TOPIC_CIRCUIT_RISK, matching the
"Early Radar" and "Circuit Risk" topics.

The token and chat-ID variables were already correct and are unchanged.

preflight() now also reports topic_sources -- which variable supplied each topic
-- so a typo in one of six secrets is visible immediately rather than causing a
silent post to the wrong place. The smoke script prints the source name and the
thread each section will land in, and lists the accepted alternatives for any
topic that is unset. Secret values are still never printed.

The test fixture cleared only one naming convention, so a value configured in the
developer's own shell could leak into a test; it now clears every accepted name.

Verified with the real secret names: all six resolve, and each section reports the
thread it will post to.

Tests: 5 new covering both conventions, precedence when both are set, and the
source reporting. 32 pass in the penny suite.
